Two different kinds of pair
---------------------------

The approved ``l026_subset_pair_family`` works with a family F={T,T^a} of
one or two subsets of the original point domain Omega. It does not compute
an orbit or relation on the unordered pairs of points in Omega.

Its mathematical criterion is the setwise stabilizer of F in the named
perfect transitive inner G. This stabilizer is proper: if G stabilized F,
its permutation image in S2 would be trivial because G is perfect. Then G
would fix the nonempty proper subset T, contradicting transitivity.
The pair role checks that a and c preserve F. If the three actual D factors
for a marking each preserve F, their ordered product b does as well.
Consequently <a,b,c> lies in that proper container. Both fix/swap parities
are valid; an outside factor or missing tag is merely inconclusive.

This criterion can cover a point-transitive proper marking group when F
is a complementary partition into two blocks of size1755. Such a group
can interchange the blocks without preserving either as a point subset.
For a transitive group preserving a family of at most two nonempty proper
subsets, this complementary case is necessary: union and intersection
are invariant point subsets. The existing generic Source admits that
case without requiring a proper union.

The currently acquired pair does not have that form. Its independent
