The proposed relation and inner-group escape
---------------------------------------------

The suggested relation certificate is mathematically valid in a more
general action. Let K<=G, and let R be a finite set of unordered pairs of
distinct points, closed under the generators of K. Complete closure makes R
K-invariant. If p belongs to R and p^g does not, for an actual known g in
the intended inner G, then g does not stabilize R. Therefore

  K <= Stab_G(R) < G.

No transitivity of G on unordered pairs is needed. If K is the rotation
group <ab,bc>, properness also excludes <a,b,c>=G, since that rotation
group is normal of index at most two in the marking group and G is perfect.
All exact membership, action and Original marking hypotheses remain needed.

An escape by an arbitrary ambient A=Aut(G) generator is insufficient:
G itself may preserve R while an outer automorphism moves it. The known
inner d0 or an accepted A-conjugate of d0 is a suitable candidate, because
G is normal in A and d0 belongs to G. Failure to find such an escape is
inconclusive, as is an incomplete relation closure.

No existing approved local L026 Source was found that implements this
general pair-relation closure plus known-inner-element escape. The current
pair kernel has only one/two Omega-subsets, no arbitrary relation carrier
and no escape predicate. Its review cannot be transferred to this different
certificate. No new implementation or guard is proposed or created here.

